{"type": "message", "id": "347565e5", "parentId": "997f45c1", "timestamp": "2026-04-16T16:40:17.035Z", "message": {"role": "toolResult", "toolCallId": "functions.web_search:2", "toolName": "web_search", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "{\n  \"query\": \"Eurostat railway suicides 2014 2020 country statistics Germany France Belgium Spain\",\n  \"provider\": \"brave\",\n  \"count\": 10,\n  \"tookMs\": 1093,\n  \"externalContent\": {\n    \"untrusted\": true,\n    \"source\": \"web_search\",\n    \"provider\": \"brave\",\n    \"wrapped\": true\n  },\n  \"results\": [\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"3bac086d5851ebc5\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nRailway safety statistics in the EU Statistics Explained\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"3bac086d5851ebc5\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://ec.europa.eu/eurostat/statistics-explained/SEPDF/cache/94376.pdf\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"4b9e4166b208dca3\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nIt should be noted that there are no railways in the EU countries Cyprus and Malta, ... The number of significant railway accidents in the EU fell almost continuously between 2010 and 2020, with the · only exceptions being <strong>a sharp increase in 2014 (+6.7%)</strong> and a slight increase in 2017 (+2.1%).\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"4b9e4166b208dca3\\\">>>\",\n      \"siteName\": \"ec.europa.eu\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"6345a410053efbdf\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\n﻿ | I Report on Railway Safety and Interoperability in the EU 2020\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"6345a410053efbdf\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://www.era.europa.eu/system/files/2022-10/Report%20on%20Railway%20Safety%20and%20Interoperability%20in%20the%20EU%202020.pdf\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"fada7ba9297ee5d3\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nFigure A-24: Suicide mortality against railway suicide rate (EU-28, 2016, 2016-18) Figure A-25: Railway employee casualties (EU-28, 2010-18) Figure A-26: Passenger and employee fatality rates (EU-28, 2006-18) Figure A-27: Level crossing accidents and resulting casualties (EU-28, 2010-18) Figure A-28: Level crossing accident rates per country (ERA countries, 2016-18) Figure A-29: Precursors to accidents (EU-28, 2014-18)\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"fada7ba9297ee5d3\\\">>>\",\n      \"siteName\": \"www.era.europa.eu\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"2f41ec0cc1b2f976\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nRailway safety statistics in the EU - Statistics Explained - Eurostat\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"2f41ec0cc1b2f976\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://ec.europa.eu/eurostat/statistics-explained/index.php?title=Railway_safety_statistics_in_the_EU\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"833512c44b3c877a\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nTable 3: Persons seriously injured ... injured in railway accidents. For the EU as a whole, the number of such suicides remained <strong>between 2 200 and 2 800 per year in the period 2010-2024</strong>....\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"833512c44b3c877a\\\">>>\",\n      \"siteName\": \"ec.europa.eu\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"95da7190f0dec09a\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\n1 EUROSTAT 2019.27.06 Rail accident fatalities in the EU\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"95da7190f0dec09a\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://www.sipotra.it/wp-content/uploads/2019/06/Rail-accident-fatalities-in-the-EU.pdf\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"fc2a8aadab64d57e\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\ninjured in derailments in 2017, ... <strong>in Belgium, two persons in · Spain and one person in Germany</strong>. Germany (88 persons seriously injured), Romania (56 persons) and · Poland (45 persons) recorded the highest numbers of persons injured in accidents to persons by rolling · stock in motion.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"fc2a8aadab64d57e\\\">>>\",\n      \"siteName\": \"www.sipotra.it\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"2c82af2ce06ed284\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nReport on Railway Safety and Interoperability in the EU - 2024\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"2c82af2ce06ed284\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://www.era.europa.eu/system/files/2024-06/Report%20on%20Railway%20Safety%20and%20Interoperability%20in%20the%20EU%202024.pdf\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"0323594b6c128a03\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nFigure A-23: Railway suicide rate (EU-27, 2011–2022) and suicide mortality rate (EU-27, 2011–2020)\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"0323594b6c128a03\\\">>>\",\n      \"siteName\": \"www.era.europa.eu\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"d1bef762fa3aeed0\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nDatabase - Transport - Eurostat - European Commission\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"d1bef762fa3aeed0\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://ec.europa.eu/eurostat/web/transport/database\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"7af51e6afc4b451b\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nLog in · English · Select your language · Close · Human translation · de Deutsch · en English · fr français · Machine translation · bg български\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"7af51e6afc4b451b\\\">>>\",\n      \"siteName\": \"ec.europa.eu\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"1918b16e5d2fa321\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nBehavioral and location‐related antecedents of train suicides - Moritz - 2023 - Suicide and Life-Threatening Behavior - Wiley Online Library\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\