{"type": "message", "id": "b918fa92", "parentId": "87bc42e0", "timestamp": "2026-04-16T16:40:42.727Z", "message": {"role": "toolResult", "toolCallId": "functions.web_search:7", "toolName": "web_search", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "{\n  \"query\": \"railway suicides statistics 2014 2020 decrease percentage by country Europe\",\n  \"provider\": \"brave\",\n  \"count\": 10,\n  \"tookMs\": 965,\n  \"externalContent\": {\n    \"untrusted\": true,\n    \"source\": \"web_search\",\n    \"provider\": \"brave\",\n    \"wrapped\": true\n  },\n  \"results\": [\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"3339c2adc829fe84\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nRailway safety statistics in the EU Statistics Explained\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"3339c2adc829fe84\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://ec.europa.eu/eurostat/statistics-explained/SEPDF/cache/94376.pdf\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"0cbf43338b70e931\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nIt should be noted that there are no railways in the EU countries Cyprus and Malta, ... The number of significant railway accidents in the EU fell almost continuously between 2010 and 2020, with the · only exceptions being <strong>a sharp increase in 2014 (+6.7%)</strong> and a slight increase in 2017 (+2.1%).\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"0cbf43338b70e931\\\">>>\",\n      \"siteName\": \"ec.europa.eu\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"c673a6df71ef8b2a\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nRail transport fatalities drop by 11% in 2024 - News articles - Eurostat\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"c673a6df71ef8b2a\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://ec.europa.eu/eurostat/web/products-eurostat-news/w/ddn-20251216-2\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"f0ed1116c009d7ec\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\n<strong>A decreasing trend was seen from 2014 to 2019, when the number fell by around 22%</strong>, and another sharp decrease of almost 15% compared with 2019 had been recorded by the end of 2021.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"f0ed1116c009d7ec\\\">>>\",\n      \"published\": \"December 16, 2025\",\n      \"siteName\": \"ec.europa.eu\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"deee6a8f96120875\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nBehavioral and location‐related antecedents of train suicides - Moritz - 2023 - Suicide and Life-Threatening Behavior - Wiley Online Library\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"deee6a8f96120875\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/10.1111/sltb.12941\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"2402de01544bc28e\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nAbstract Background In the European Union, <strong>over 2000 suicides on railway premises were reported in 2020.</strong> Identifying individuals&#x27; behavioral and location patterns just before they die or attempt to...\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"2402de01544bc28e\\\">>>\",\n      \"published\": \"January 30, 2023\",\n      \"siteName\": \"onlinelibrary.wiley.com\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"251567ebfaca01d8\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\n<span class=\\\"mw-page-title-main\\\">Railway safety statistics in the EU</span>\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"251567ebfaca01d8\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://ec.europa.eu/eurostat/statistics-explained/index.php?title=Railway_safety_statistics_in_the_EU\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"be061aadbd8a936a\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nIt should be noted that there are no railways in the EU countries Cyprus and Malta, nor in the EEA/EFTA country Iceland. The number of significant railway accidents in the EU fell almost continuously between 2010 and 2020, with the only exceptions being <strong>a sharp increase in 2014 (+6.7%)</strong> and a slight ...\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"be061aadbd8a936a\\\">>>\",\n      \"siteName\": \"ec.europa.eu\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"fbdd6ce6312ad657\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nAssessment of the Impact of Rail Suicides on EU Railways\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"fbdd6ce6312ad657\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://www.era.europa.eu/system/files/2022-10/Report%20on%20assessment%20of%20the%20impact%20of%20rail%20suicides%20on%20EU%20railways.pdf\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"860bea05722796d7\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nThe European Union Agency for Railways (ERA) facilitates the development of the Single European Railway Area. It enhances interoperability, harmonises rules, and promotes safety. Since June 2019, ERA issues safety certificates and vehicle authorisations valid across multiple European countries.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"860bea05722796d7\\\">>>\",\n      \"siteName\": \"www.era.europa.eu\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"ea842b16d953c67a\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nUQAM | CRISE | Railway suicides | Railway suicide in the world\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"ea842b16d953c67a\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://railwaysuicideprevention.com/railway-fatalities/railway-suicide-in-the-world.html\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"2beecdc338e8c731\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nIn order to properly compare countries in terms of their suicide mortality, it would be necessary to develop standardised indicators and data collection tools. However, some elements can be identified for comparison in various studies across the world.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"2beecdc338e8c731\\\">>>\",\n      \"siteName\": \"railwaysuicideprevention.com\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \