{"type": "message", "id": "b5237c5e", "parentId": "58854445", "timestamp": "2026-04-16T16:41:40.919Z", "message": {"role": "toolResult", "toolCallId": "functions.web_search:15", "toolName": "web_search", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "{\n  \"query\": \"site:ec.europa.eu eurostat railway suicides country data table 2014 2020\",\n  \"provider\": \"brave\",\n  \"count\": 10,\n  \"tookMs\": 978,\n  \"externalContent\": {\n    \"untrusted\": true,\n    \"source\": \"web_search\",\n    \"provider\": \"brave\",\n    \"wrapped\": true\n  },\n  \"results\": [\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"0a5f7f9e1b969c70\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nRailway safety statistics in the EU Statistics Explained\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"0a5f7f9e1b969c70\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://ec.europa.eu/eurostat/statistics-explained/SEPDF/cache/94376.pdf\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"144769984f95bef7\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nIt should be noted that there are no railways in the EU countries Cyprus and Malta, ... The number of significant railway accidents in the EU fell almost continuously between 2010 and 2020, with the · only exceptions being <strong>a sharp increase in 2014 (+6.7%)</strong> and a slight increase in 2017 (+2.1%).\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"144769984f95bef7\\\">>>\",\n      \"siteName\": \"ec.europa.eu\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"06ed9c0d9472f441\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nRail transport fatalities drop by 11% in 2024 - News articles - Eurostat\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"06ed9c0d9472f441\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://ec.europa.eu/eurostat/web/products-eurostat-news/w/ddn-20251216-2\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"f771642045c27fe1\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nIn 2024, <strong>the highest number of people killed in railway accidents was recorded in Poland (163 fatalities), followed by Germany (142) and Romania (65)</strong>. On the other end, the lowest numbers were observed in Luxembourg and Slovenia (where in fact ...\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"f771642045c27fe1\\\">>>\",\n      \"published\": \"December 16, 2025\",\n      \"siteName\": \"ec.europa.eu\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"173d90bbb63533cd\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nRailway safety statistics in the EU - Statistics Explained - Eurostat\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"173d90bbb63533cd\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://ec.europa.eu/eurostat/statistics-explained/index.php?title=Railway_safety_statistics_in_the_EU\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"1faec2a867122a2c\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nIt should be noted that there are no railways in the EU countries Cyprus and Malta, nor in the EEA/EFTA country Iceland. The number of significant railway accidents in the EU fell almost continuously between 2010 and 2020, with the only exceptions being <strong>a sharp increase in 2014 (+6.7%)</strong> and a slight ...\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"1faec2a867122a2c\\\">>>\",\n      \"siteName\": \"ec.europa.eu\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"c87eadc0d3719fb7\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nSuicides involving railways - Statistics | Eurostat\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"c87eadc0d3719fb7\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://ec.europa.eu/eurostat/databrowser/product/page/TRAN_SF_RAILSU\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"c8b6db350b31f4ff\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nWe cannot provide a description for this page right now\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"c8b6db350b31f4ff\\\">>>\",\n      \"siteName\": \"ec.europa.eu\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"106897a57356cd9a\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\n[tran_sf_railsu] Suicides involving railways\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"106897a57356cd9a\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://ec.europa.eu/eurostat/databrowser/product/view/tran_sf_railsu\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"c3438eebdc8df7e0\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nWe cannot provide a description for this page right now\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"c3438eebdc8df7e0\\\">>>\",\n      \"siteName\": \"ec.europa.eu\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"cd5891fed1141c2c\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nDatabase - Transport - Eurostat - European Commission\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"cd5891fed1141c2c\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://ec.europa.eu/eurostat/web/transport/database\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"c591ca287620c133\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nLog in · English · Select your language · Close · Human translation · de Deutsch · en English · fr français · Machine translation · bg български\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"c591ca287620c133\\\">>>\",\n      \"siteName\": \"ec.europa.eu\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"4763ea2fc015cd1a\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nSearch results for \\\"유로컵 참가국-（H87.CC）-유로컵 참가국->>h87.cc<<-h0neo.html\\\" - Statistics Explained - Eurostat\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"4763ea2fc015cd1a\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://ec.europa.eu/eurostat/statistics-explained/index.php/Railway_safety_statistics_in_the_EU\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"b82f4cb363d577ae\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nRetrieved from &quot;https://ec.europa.eu/eurostat/statistics-explained/index.php?title=Special:Search&quot;\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"b82f4cb363d577ae\\\">>>\",\n      \"siteName\": \"ec.europa.eu\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"0f0c87212f133285\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nDeaths in rail accidents down to 687 in 2020 - Products Eurostat News - Eurostat\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"0f0c87212f133285\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://ec.europa.eu/eurostat/web/products-eurostat-news/-/ddn-20220113-1\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"e78555ee1dd05e41\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nA total of <strong>687 people were killed</strong> and 468 were seriously injured in these accidents in 2020 (excl. suicides), with both numbers generally falling since 2010. This information comes from data on railway safety published by Eurostat today.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"e78555ee1dd05e41\\\">>>\",\n      \"published\": \"January 13, 2022\",\n      \"siteName\": \"ec.europa.eu\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"85cb5478579ec8b6\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nRailway safety statistics in the EU - European Commission\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"85cb5478579ec8b6\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://ec.europa.eu/eurostat/statistics-explained/index.php/Rail_accident_fatalities_in_the_EU\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"c141ac5a19a262ae\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nWith 2 379 reported cases in 2018, ... by ERA. ... The number of significant railway accidents fell between 2010 and 2018, with the exception of <strong>two increases in 2014</strong> ......\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"c141ac5a19a262ae\\\">>>\",\n      \"siteName\": \"ec.europa.eu\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"60684365694f73d0\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nRail transport safety (tran_sf_rail) - European Union\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"60684365694f73d0\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://ec.europa.eu/eurostat/cache/metadata/en/tran_sf_rail_esms.htm\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"a966c0a713e1e019\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nThe rail accident data are provided to Eurostat by the European Union Agency for Railways (ERA). The ERA manages and is responsible for the entire data collection. The Eurostat data constitute a part of the data collected by ERA and are part of the so-called Common Safety Indicators (CSIs). In Eurobase, the following data are available: ... Number of suicides involving railways.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"a966c0a713e1e019\\\">>>\",\n      \"siteName\": \"ec.europa.eu\"\n    }\n  ]\n}"}], "details": {"query": "site:ec.europa.eu eurostat railway suicides country data table 2014 2020", "provider": "brave", "count": 10, "tookMs": 978, "externalContent": {"untrusted": true, "source": "web_search", "provider": "brave", "wrapped": true}, "results": [{"title": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"0a5f7f9e1b969c70\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nRailway safety statistics in the EU Statistics Explained\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"0a5f7f9e1b969c70\">>>", "url": "https://ec.europa.eu/eurostat/statistics-explained/SEPDF/cache/94376.pdf", "description": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"144769984f95bef7\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nIt should be noted that there are no railways in the EU countries Cyprus and Malta, ... The number of significant railway accidents in the EU fell almost continuously between 2010 and 2020, with the · only exceptions being <strong>a sharp increase in 2014 (+6.7%)</strong> and a slight increase in 2017 (+2.1%).\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"144769984f95bef7\">>>", "siteName": "ec.europa.eu"}, {"title": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"06ed9c0d9472f441\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nRail transport fatalities drop by 11% in 2024 - News articles - Eurostat\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"06ed9c0d9472f441\">>>", "url": "https://ec.europa.eu/eurostat/web/products-eu