{"type": "message", "id": "ab394481", "parentId": "a6c452a3", "timestamp": "2026-04-16T16:43:53.821Z", "message": {"role": "toolResult", "toolCallId": "functions.web_search:23", "toolName": "web_search", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "{\n  \"query\": \"railway suicide prevention Europe country comparison 2014 2020\",\n  \"provider\": \"brave\",\n  \"count\": 10,\n  \"tookMs\": 987,\n  \"externalContent\": {\n    \"untrusted\": true,\n    \"source\": \"web_search\",\n    \"provider\": \"brave\",\n    \"wrapped\": true\n  },\n  \"results\": [\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"702ed64033b20606\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\n﻿ | I Report on Railway Safety and Interoperability in the EU 2020\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"702ed64033b20606\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://www.era.europa.eu/system/files/2022-10/Report%20on%20Railway%20Safety%20and%20Interoperability%20in%20the%20EU%202020.pdf\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"84c4865a82ec672e\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nFigure A-24: Suicide mortality against railway suicide rate (EU-28, 2016, 2016-18) Figure A-25: Railway employee casualties (EU-28, 2010-18) Figure A-26: Passenger and employee fatality rates (EU-28, 2006-18) Figure A-27: Level crossing accidents and resulting casualties (EU-28, 2010-18) Figure A-28: Level crossing accident rates per country (ERA countries, 2016-18) Figure A-29: Precursors to accidents (EU-28, 2014...\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"84c4865a82ec672e\\\">>>\",\n      \"siteName\": \"www.era.europa.eu\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"8483665774a4c025\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nRailway safety statistics in the EU Statistics Explained\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"8483665774a4c025\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://ec.europa.eu/eurostat/statistics-explained/SEPDF/cache/94376.pdf\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"115106832f72cd8e\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nIt should be noted that there are no railways in the EU countries Cyprus and Malta, ... The number of significant railway accidents in the EU fell almost continuously between 2010 and 2020, with the · only exceptions being <strong>a sharp increase in 2014 (+6.7%)</strong> and a slight increase in 2017 (+2.1%).\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"115106832f72cd8e\\\">>>\",\n      \"siteName\": \"ec.europa.eu\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"164a1f2275d27f05\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nRail transport fatalities drop by 11% in 2024 - News articles - Eurostat\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"164a1f2275d27f05\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://ec.europa.eu/eurostat/web/products-eurostat-news/w/ddn-20251216-2\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"d24790a2e1b6c27e\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nThe number of suicides on railways is constantly much higher than the number of fatalities despite the downward trend seen in the EU the past decade <strong>(2 357 in 2024 compared with 2 608 in 2014, -9.6%)</strong>.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"d24790a2e1b6c27e\\\">>>\",\n      \"published\": \"December 16, 2025\",\n      \"siteName\": \"ec.europa.eu\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"ac952c42d5ca68e5\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nFull article: Environmental Risk Factors for Railway Suicide: A Nationwide Analysis of England’s Mainline Network (2019–2021)\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"ac952c42d5ca68e5\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://www.tandfonline.com/doi/full/10.1080/13811118.2025.2595428\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"cbc6aafd16ea8c26\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nRestricting access to high-speed trains—especially at smaller urban stations and at non-station locations—could be an effective element of broader strategies and local partnership approaches to prevent suicide. In England, most railway suicides (especially at stations) occur in urban areas · Most people died near home, but often not at their nearest station · Fast trains at nearby stations predicted death at station vs. non-station locations ... In many countries, suicide is the leading cause of death on the railway networks (European Union Agency for Railways, Citation2018).\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"cbc6aafd16ea8c26\\\">>>\",\n      \"siteName\": \"www.tandfonline.com\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"dbada8fc4cbe74ac\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\n<span class=\\\"mw-page-title-main\\\">Railway safety statistics in the EU</span>\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"dbada8fc4cbe74ac\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://ec.europa.eu/eurostat/statistics-explained/index.php?title=Railway_safety_statistics_in_the_EU\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"17545e0c3fb1bec0\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nThe highest decrease was observed between 2012 and 2013 (-6.7%) while the highest increase was observed between 2021 and 2022 (+7.5%). <strong>The number of suicides on railway premises has fallen consistently from 2017 to 2020 but registered a slight increase in 2021 (+1.4%)</strong>.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"17545e0c3fb1bec0\\\">>>\",\n      \"siteName\": \"ec.europa.eu\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"755aa2c8fc00cf5f\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nReport on Railway Safety and Interoperability in the EU - 2024\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"755aa2c8fc00cf5f\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://www.era.europa.eu/system/files/2024-06/Report%20on%20Railway%20Safety%20and%20Interoperability%20in%20the%20EU%202024.pdf\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"a5808932cccd7da8\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nFigure A-24: Suicide mortality rate compared with railway suicide rate (EU-27 + CH + NO) Figure A-25: Railway employee casualties (EU-27, 2010–2022) Figure A-26: Railway passenger and employee fatality rates (EU-27, 2006–2022) Figure A-27: Level crossing accidents and resulting casualties (EU-27, 2010–2022) Figure A-28: Level crossing accident rates (EU-27 + CH + NO, 2020–2022) Figure A-29: Precursors to accidents (EU-27, 2018–2022) Figure A-30: Accident precursor to accident ratio per country (EU-27 + CH + NO, 2018–2022)\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"a5808932cccd7da8\\\">>>\",\n      \"siteName\": \"www.era.europa.eu\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"b419af956d8e6639\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nSystematic review of research on railway and urban transit system suicides - ScienceDirect\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"b419af956d8e6639\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/abs/pii/S0165032715310119\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"cbd719b5da1897d8\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nBackground: Suicides in the railway system is a serious health, societal, and transportation concern. Restriction of the access to suicide methods in the form of different physical barriers is a promising approach for suicide prevention. Method: Mid-track fencing, which is fencing placed in-between the high-speed and commuter train tracks, was installed at one out of seven stations along a train line outside of Stockholm in the years 2013/2014.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"cbd719b5da1897d8\\\">>>\",\n      \"published\": \"December 29, 2015\",\n      \"siteName\": \"www.sciencedirect.com\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"34b8a8f70c450bfc\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nBehavioral and location‐related antecedents of train suicides - Moritz - 2023 - Suicide and Life-Threatening Behavior - Wiley Online Library\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"34b8a8f70c450bfc\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/10.1111/sltb.12941\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"c13103b82d002d99\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nIn the European Union, <strong>over 2000 suicides on railway premises were reported in 2020.</strong> Identifying individuals&#x27; behavioral and location patterns just before they die or attempt to die by train suicide (ITS) is critical for effective prevention ...\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"c13103b82d002d99\\\">>>\",\n      \"published\": \"January 30, 2023\",\n      \"siteName\": \"onlinelibrary.wiley.com\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"29a669f6aa61ac16\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nUQAM | CRISE | Railway suicides | Railway suicide in the world\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"29a669f6aa61ac16\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://railwaysuicideprevention.com/railway-fatalities/railway-suicide-in-the-world.html\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"e1a26a0f82e97dc8\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nRailway suicides vary from country to country. Therefore, one has to be very careful when drawing conclusions from analyses and preventive measures that have been developed elsewhere. It is also important to note that data in different countries do not necessarily use the same criteria for ...\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"e1a26a0f82e97dc8\\\">>>\",\n      \"siteName\": \"railwaysuicideprevention.com\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"2b739c44f920c18b\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nStrategies for Reducing Suicide at Railroads: A Scoping Review of Evidence and Gaps - PMC\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"2b739c44f920c18b\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC11765353/\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"7f3ce058324710e5\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nDistribution of 26 studies related to railways across ten countries. ... Histogram of publication years for the 26 evaluated manuscripts on prevention strategies related to railways. ... Histogram of average year of intervention implementation for 26 included studies. Quantitative findings were sparse across all interventions, as empirical studies typically concentrated on specific train lines or city regions and assessed only a small number of suicides.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"7f3ce058324710e5\\\">>>\",\n      \"siteName\": \"pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov\"\n    }\n  ]\n}"}], "details": {"query": "railway suicide prevention Europe country comparison 2014 2020", "provider": "brave", "count": 10, "tookMs": 987, "externalContent": {"untrusted": true, "source": "web_search", "provider": "brave", "wrapped": true}, "results": [{"title": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"702ed64033b20606\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\n﻿ | I Report on Railway Safety and Interoperability in the EU 2020\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"702ed64033b20606\">>>", "url": "https://www.era.europa.eu/system/files/2022-10/Report%20on%20Railway%20Safety%20and%20Interoperability%20in%20the%20EU%202020.pdf", "description": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"84c4865a82ec672e\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nFigure A-24: Suicide mortality against railway suicide rate (EU-28, 2016, 2016-18) Figure A-25: Railway employee casualties (EU-28, 2010-18) Figure A-26: Passenger and employee fatality rates (EU-28, 2006-18) Figure A-27: Level crossing accidents and resulting casualties (EU-28, 2010-18) Figure A-28: Level crossing accident rates per country (ERA countries, 2016-18) Figure A-29: Precursors to accidents (EU-28, 2014...\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"84c4865a82ec672e\">>>", "siteName": "www.era.europa.eu"}, {"title": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"8483665774a4c025\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nRailway safety statistics in the EU Statistics Explained\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"8483665774a4c025\">>>", "url": "https://ec.europa.eu/eurostat/statistics-explained/SEPDF/cache/94376.pdf", "description": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"115106832f72cd8e\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nIt should be noted that there are no railways in the EU countries Cyprus and Malta, ... The number of significant railway accidents in the EU fell almost continuously between 2010 and 2020, with the · only exceptions being <strong>a sharp increase in 2014 (+6.7%)</strong> and a slight increase in 2017 (+2.1%).\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"115106832f72cd8e\">>>", "siteName": "ec.europa.eu"}, {"title": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"164a1f2275d27f05\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nRail transport fatalities drop by 11% in 2024 - News articles - Eurostat\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"164a1f2275d27f05\">>>", "url": "https://ec.europa.eu/eurostat/web/products-eurostat-news/w/ddn-20251216-2", "description": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"d24790a2e1b6c27e\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nThe number of suicides on railways is constantly much higher than the number of fatalities despite the downward trend seen in the EU the past decade <strong>(2 357 in 2024 compared with 2 608 in 2014, -9.6%)</strong>.\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"d24790a2e1b6c27e\">>>", "published": "December 16, 2025", "siteName": "ec.europa.eu"}, {"title": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"ac952c42d5ca68e5\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nFull article: Environmental Risk Factors for Railway Suicide: A Nationwide Analysis of England’s Mainline Network (2019–2021)\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"ac952c42d5ca68e5\">>>", "url": "https://www.tandfonline.com/doi/full/10.1080/13811118.2025.2595428", "description": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"cbc6aafd16ea8c26\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nRestricting access to high-speed trains—especially at smaller urban stations and at non-station locations—could be an effective element of broader strategies and local partnership approaches to prevent suicide. In England, most railway suicides (especially at stations) occur in urban areas · Most people died near home, but often not at their nearest station · Fast trains at nearby stations predicted death at station vs. non-station locations ... In many countries, suicide is the leading cause of death on the railway networks (European Union Agency for Railways, Citation2018).\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"cbc6aafd16ea8c26\">>>", "siteName": "www.tandfonline.com"}, {"title": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"dbada8fc4cbe74ac\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\n<span class=\"mw-page-title-main\">Railway safety statistics in the EU</span>\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"dbada8fc4cbe74ac\">>>", "url": "https://ec.europa.eu/eurostat/statistics-explained/index.php?title=Railway_safety_statistics_in_the_EU", "description": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"17545e0c3fb1bec0\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nThe highest decrease was observed between 2012 and 2013 (-6.7%) while the highest increase was observed between 2021 and 2022 (+7.5%). <strong>The number of suicides on railway premises has fallen consistently from 2017 to 2020 but registered a slight increase in 2021 (+1.4%)</strong>.\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"17545e0c3fb1bec0\">>>", "siteName": "ec.europa.eu"}, {"title": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"755aa2c8fc00cf5f\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nReport on Railway Safety and Interoperability in the EU - 2024\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"755aa2c8fc00cf5f\">>>", "url": "https://www.era.europa.eu/system/files/2024-06/Report%20on%20Railway%20Safety%20and%20Interoperability%20in%20the%20EU%202024.pdf", "description": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"a5808932cccd7da8\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nFigure A-24