idents and resulting casualties (EU-27, 2010–2022) Figure A-28: Level crossing accident rates (EU-27 + CH + NO, 2020–2022)\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"f81eeec81f90e06a\\\">>>\",\n      \"siteName\": \"www.era.europa.eu\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"f36ba9ddbba81419\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\n1 EUROSTAT 2019.27.06 Rail accident fatalities in the EU\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"f36ba9ddbba81419\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://www.sipotra.it/wp-content/uploads/2019/06/Rail-accident-fatalities-in-the-EU.pdf\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"ef883a5b3816745a\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nWith <strong>2 773 reported cases in 2017,</strong> suicides · outnumber the victims accounted for by railway accidents. Eurostat publishes data collected by the European Railway Agency (ERA) in Eurobase. This ... total of 1 855 accidents (+3.8 %) (Figure 1). Nevertheless, railway safety has generally improved ...\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"ef883a5b3816745a\\\">>>\",\n      \"siteName\": \"www.sipotra.it\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"fdc6c48803839aa8\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nUQAM | CRISE | Railway suicides | Railway suicide in the world\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"fdc6c48803839aa8\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://railwaysuicideprevention.com/railway-fatalities/railway-suicide-in-the-world.html\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"223a73a58c6981aa\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nLast update: Aug. 2018 · Railway suicides vary from country to country. Therefore, one has to be very careful when drawing conclusions from analyses and preventive measures that have been developed elsewhere. It is also important to note that data in different countries do not necessarily ...\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"223a73a58c6981aa\\\">>>\",